{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/tokenExchange(subjectToken:subjectTokenType:actorToken:scopes:audience:resource:tenantID:configuration:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"code":"POST \/oauth2\/token","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the RFC 8693 grant (§15.1).","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tokenExchange","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"subjectToken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Sensitive","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"subjectTokenType","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"actorToken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/Sensitive","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scopes","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"audience","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resource","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tenantID","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"configuration","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OidcConfiguration","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK17OidcConfigurationV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcConfiguration","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ExchangedToken","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK14ExchangedTokenV","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ExchangedToken","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the token being exchanged — positional and first, because four"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional strings in positional order is a bug waiting to be written."}]}],"name":"subjectToken"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"what kind of token "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subjectToken"},{"type":"text","text":" is. "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Required"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" (§15.1), with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no default: a default would be this SDK choosing which kind of credential the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"caller holds, which is what §15.7 forbids. Pass "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/accessTokenType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same-domain exchange, or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/jwtTokenType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for a trusted external issuer’s JWT"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(§15.7). This SDK never reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subjectToken"},{"type":"text","text":" to decide the value: which kind of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"token the caller holds is only the caller’s to know, AXIAM refuses refresh and ID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"token types by name, and a refusal is never retried as a different type."}]}],"name":"subjectTokenType"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"its presence selects delegation; its absence selects impersonation."}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Two different operations with different risk, and §15.2 rule 1 forbids papering over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the difference: this SDK supplies no default actor token and never substitutes its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own session for one. Passing nothing here asks for impersonation, and the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refuses unless this client holds that grant."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The actor token must have been issued to this client"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" (§15.2 rule 9, contract"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"1.60): obtain it with the same client’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient\/loginClientCredentials(scope:tenantID:configuration:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grant and pass its "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcTokenSet\/accessToken","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" here — its "},{"code":"sub","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is this client’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"client_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A token issued to another client, a console sign-in or a service"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"account is answered "},{"code":"400","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"invalid_request","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (“actor_token was not issued to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exchanging client”), which surfaces unchanged: not retried, not rewritten into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"impersonation, and not repaired by substituting a token of this SDK’s own."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"actorToken"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"omit to inherit the subject’s, bounded by this client’s registration. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"response’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ExchangedToken\/scope","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is what was actually granted, which may be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"narrower than what was asked for even on success (§15.2 rule 7) — read it.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"scopes"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What this deliberately does "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" do:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"No retry, downgrade or rewrite on ","type":"text"},{"code":"unauthorized_client","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (§15.2 rule 2). It means"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"either “this client may not exchange at all” or “this client may not impersonate”;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"both are registration facts an operator must fix, and reworking the request into a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delegation would send one the caller did not write."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"No auto-narrowing on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"invalid_scope"}]},{"text":" (§15.2 rule 3). The server refuses rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"silently narrowing precisely so the caller finds out here.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"No refresh token, ever","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (§15.2 rule 4). ","type":"text"},{"code":"TokenExchangeResponse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has no such field,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ExchangedToken","type":"reference"},{"text":" has nowhere to put one, and this result never enters the §9","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single-flight refresh guard. Re-run the exchange to get a fresh token.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"No adoption","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (§15.2 rule 5). The exchanged token is not this client’s session — not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"even behind an opt-in flag, which is a MUST NOT here where adoption elsewhere is a MAY.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It is a token to hand onward in one outbound call; adopting it would silently","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"re-privilege every subsequent call this client makes.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A cross-tenant subject token answers "},{"code":"invalid_grant","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and this SDK does not try to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"distinguish “wrong tenant” from “bad token” (§15.3): the server collapses them because"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"telling them apart is a tenant-enumeration signal."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/axiamclient\/tokenexchange(subjecttoken:subjecttokentype:actortoken:scopes:audience:resource:tenantid:configuration:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK0A6ClientC13tokenExchange12subjectToken0fG4Type05actorG06scopes8audience8resource8tenantID13configurationAA09ExchangedG0VAA9SensitiveVySSG_SSAQSgSaySSGSgSSSgA2uA17OidcConfigurationVSgtYaKF","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tokenExchange","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"subjectToken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"subjectTokenType","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"actorToken","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sensitive","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK9SensitiveV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"scopes","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"audience","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","precis